%S A137313 1,2,3,5,6,7,10,11,13,17,23,26,27,30,33,35,37,38,45,46,47,58,61,62,63,
%T A137313 70,73,77,81,83,87,90,91,101,102,103,107,110,115,118,121,122,125,126,
%U A137313 131,137,138,142,143,146,147,151,161,165,166,170,173,175,177,178
%N A137313 Numbers k such that a type-6 Gaussian normal basis over GF(2^k) exists.
%C A137313 A type-t Gaussian normal basis exists for GF(2^k) if and only if p = k*t+1 is prime and gcd(k, (p-1)/ord(2 mod p)) = 1.
%C A137313 From _Jianing Song_, Oct 06 2026: (Start)
%C A137313 Note that p = k*t+1 being prime and gcd(k, (p-1)/ord(2 mod p)) = 1 imply that (p-1)/ord(2 mod p) divides t. In particular, k is a term in this sequence if and only if k satisfies one the following conditions:
%C A137313 (i) ord(2 mod p) = p-1 (k = 2, 3, 6, 10, 11, ...);
%C A137313 (ii) k odd, and ord(2 mod p) = (p-1)/2 (k = 1, 13, 17, 33, 45, ...);
%C A137313 (iii) k is not divisible by 3, and ord(2 mod p) = (p-1)/3 (k = 7, 26, 38, 46, 47, ...);
%C A137313 (iv) k is not divisible by 2 or 3, and ord(2 mod p) = (p-1)/6 (k = 5, 37, 73, 121, 221, ...). (End)
%H A137313 Jianing Song, <a href="/A137313/b137313.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A137313 Joerg Arndt, <a href="https://www.jjj.de/fxt/#fxtbook">Matters Computational (The Fxtbook)</a>, section 42.9 "Gaussian normal bases", pp.914-920.
%o A137313 (PARI) istypet(n,t=6) = my(p); (isprime(p=n*t+1) && gcd(n, (p-1)/znorder(Mod(2, p))) == 1) \\ _Jianing Song_, Oct 06 2026, following _Michel Marcus_'s program in A101284
%Y A137313 Cf. A071642 (type-1), A054639 (type-2), A136415 (type-3), A137310 (type-4), A137311 (type-5), A137314 (type-7), A101284 (type-8).
%K A137313 nonn,changed
